  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Menton is an exception on the Côte d'Azur: the town hall lists three beaches specially set up to welcome dogs. Hawaï beach, towards Garavan, a stone's throw from the Italian border, is the one this listing covers: a pebble beach with views over the hills.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>In its press release of 29 April 2026 ("Dogs on Menton's beaches: reminder of the rules in force"), the town lists three beaches set up for dogs: Gorbio beach (at the Roquebrune-Cap-Martin boundary), Casino beach and Hawaï beach (Garavan). It also states that the municipal police ran a week of prevention with dog owners, followed by fines for non-compliance. Its "Le bord de mer, les plages" page specifies that all the other beaches are banned to animals, even on a leash. We found no official source on possible hours or a seasonal period: ask the town hall, and keep your dog on a leash as a precaution.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the Garavan area is also very close to Italy — a good way to turn your walk into a two-country outing on the same day.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Casino beach, more central, and Gorbio beach are the other two beaches the town hall lists for dogs. The Pointe des Douaniers beach in Cap-d'Ail is a few kilometres west.</p>
    </div>

